Recently, my laptop froze and I needed to pull the plug. I couldn't
boot up anymore (with any kernel), so I threw together an initrd with
the btrfs utilities and boot into that.

btrfsck -s 1, 2 and 3 all gave errors
So I decided to do a btrfs-zero-log and now my FS is
mountable/bootable again. It works just like it did before, but the
errors from btrfsck are still there.

I know the current btrfsck is readonly, but are these errors already
fixable by Chris' current code?


